      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "Was marked before as \"Available In Future Release\" by internal task tracking process, but actually \"Closed\" fits better. This is caused by using the popular \"GoGo Loco\" locomotion prefab on an avatar. It sets the hips tracking control to \"Animation\" only when in FBT. If you want your avatar to not have head bobbing during running, that would have to be set to \"Tracking\" instead. For GoGo Loco, it's set in the GoLocoBase.controller in the Locomotion layer, in the \"( 5+ pt )\" state machine, within which is the \"FBT Motion\" state, which has the VRC Animator Tracking Control state behavior, which is setting \"Hip\" to \"Animation\" changing that to \"Tracking\" would cause the head to no longer bob up and down.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
